  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Generally dry weather through next weekend. \nDrought conditions will worsen.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nDry weather now looks to persist through the end of next \nweekend. \n\nA cold front moves through today with a very fractured line of\nshowers accompanying it through, mainly over the north this\nmorning. Looking at Sunday/s 18z raob from KCAR tells you pretty\nmuch everything that needs to be said. The PW value was 0.18 \ninches. The all time minimum for PW for 10/25 at KCAR is 0.15 \ninches. Current Total PW from GOES-East as of 04z only ranges\nfrom 0.80-0.90 inches along the front. This does not give much\nhope for wetting rainfall at any point today but cannot rule out\na few hundredths on inch falling in some locations, those most\nplaces will end up being skunked.\n\nCAA will keep temps in the 40s on Tuesday with brisk northwest\nwinds expected. Afternoon relative humidities will be quite low\nand range from 30-40% on both Tuesday and Wednesday. \n\nExpect temps to moderate through the end of week with highs\napproaching 60 once again on Thursday with a cold front moving\nthru Thursday night into Friday. This front holds a little bit\nbetter promise for rain over the north but has certainly trended\ndrier than it showed several days prior. \n\nAll in all, it appears that the drought worsens through next\nweekend with no guarantee for any wet weather at this time.",
